X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Mountains To Sea Trail Hiking Club": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiking-club/events/317507361/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_mountains_to_sea_trail_hiking_club
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_317507361@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261128T072759Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T110000
SUMMARY:Craven Gap
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly undulating hike. It's narrow at first with some rocky steps and then 
 narrow and rooty for most of the way until halfway when there's a short cl
 imb to the 2.5 mile mark. We go about 2.7 to 2.9 mph.\n\nWell behaved dogs
  on leashes are welcome to attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel
  lot on the other side of the road\, closest to Town Mountain. You'll see 
 some people gathering by their cars.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are d
 esigned for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably 
 fit. It's not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we ca
 n get our hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversati
 on and meet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce o
 urselves briefly. There will be a person who is a sweep. This person is th
 e person who walks last and makes sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the p
 arking spot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature break\, we wait fo you\, bu
 t it's not a hike where we stop and take photos or frequent breaks. We bas
 ically keep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then turn around after a short
  (approximately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that same pace on the way ba
 ck. If we get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are normally finished around 1
 0:50.\n\nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning that we hike in and turn a
 round half way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/317507361/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261120T005443Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T005443Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Ashevillehikinggroup": "https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/317528763/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_317528763@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261128T072758Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261130T123000
SUMMARY:Givens
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThe last time we did this was in J
 uly 2025 when Craig brought over a bunch of folks. No one had hiked here b
 efore\, and everyone thoroughly enjoyed it. After 6 weeks off\, I thorough
 ly enjoy it\, too. After another 6-week recovery\, it’s time to return t
 o leading again.\n\nGivens trails\, the hiking of which kept me sane (deba
 table) over the past 6 weeks\, are cut into the east slope of Busby mounta
 ins. These are not easy trails\, lots of ups and downs\; but\, it’s a sh
 ort hike: 5.5 miles\, pace of 2 to 2.5 mph. This area is fully wooded\, bu
 t leaves are off\, so early winter views with two unobstructed and excelle
 nt long-range views: Spivey Mtn and Pisgah Mtn. The grounds crew\, good pe
 ople those folks\, blew the leaves off all the trails prior to Thanksgivin
 g.\n\n**Entering the property**: There is a guard shack and gates. These a
 re designed to keep you out. The management team calls this area the “We
 lcome Center.” After entering the property from Sweeten Creek Rd\, **tak
 e the left lane next to the guard shack** and tell the guard that you are 
 hiking with Todd Butler\, Asbury Commons. Trailhead is Cokesbury Lane. [If
  both gates are open just drive to the trailhead. No need to stop.]\n\n**D
 irections to trailhead:** After the “Welcome Center\,” take the first 
 right onto Wesley Drive to the first stop sign and turn right onto Far Hor
 izon Lane and immediately afterwards keep straight onto Cokesbury Lane. Go
  almost to the cul-de-sac and park head-in on the left. Look for the greyi
 ng and aging hike leader beside the grey and aging Toyota Tacoma. Bunch of
  spaces across from duplexes 510-515. Not unlimited parking\, so number of
  hikers limited. If sighted\, pls don’t run over the turkeys. They think
  they are important.\n\n**Dogs**: pre-approved dogs\, a new concept\, only
 . Dogs must keep their owners on leash. \;-) Givens rules\; not mine.\n\n*
 *People:** This is my home\; ergo\, I must know you and have hiked with yo
 u in order for you to sign up. Thank you for understanding.\n\nNo AI was u
 sed in writing this overly long and wordy description. Perhaps I should ha
 ve used it?
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/317528763
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261121T185324Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261121T185324Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
