BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/birding-for-beginners-jan-27/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270105T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270105T103000
DTSTAMP:20261104T184608Z
CREATED:20261104T184608Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T184608Z
UID:1778780020265-1799139600-1799145000@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Birding for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:Birding for Beginners\nwith Shane Myers \nTuesday\, January 5  |  9 – 10:30 am \nBRN – Elective \nRegister Here!\nStarting in the classroom\, you will get a chance to learn best practices for using binoculars\, try out spotting scopes\, and look at different field guides. Later in class\, we’ll move outside and practice observing birds around the buildings and core garden area. Bring your own binoculars but if you do not have a pair\, we have some loaner binoculars available to use during the program. \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nShane Myers’ interest in nature began as a child with a love of dinosaurs. This quickly grew to include fossils\, insects\, and reptiles\, and learning from the notes his grandparents kept of the birds that came to their feeders in Toledo\, Ohio.  He has a Bachelors of Science in Wildlife Biology and did most of his undergraduate work on dragonflies and damselflies. He’s assisted in outreach and education for plant conservation groups\, Odonata Groups\, and various bird groups. Shane currently works for the Adult Education department at the NC Arboretum. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/birding-for-beginners-jan-27/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education,BRN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/20180402_btynan_Downy-Woodpecker_7447.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/botanical-drawing-beginners-jan-27/2027-01-05/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270105T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270105T123000
DTSTAMP:20261104T173328Z
CREATED:20261104T173328Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T173328Z
UID:1778780020252-1799141400-1799152200@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Botanical Drawing for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:Botanical Drawing for Beginners\nwith Camille Daunno \nFour Sessions: \nTuesdays\, January 5\, 12\, 19\, and 26 | 9:30 am – 12:30 pm \nRegister Here!\nDiscover the fundamentals of botanical drawing in this welcoming beginner-level class. During this four-week series students will learn essential drawing techniques including contour drawing\, line work\, shading and texture. Through guided instruction and observation\, students will build confidence in capturing the shapes\, patterns\, and details found in nature while developing their own artistic style. All materials are provided\, and participants will leave with in-progress and completed works as well as new skills to continue their botanical drawing practice at home. \nCamille Daunno is a retired Art Teacher with an undergraduate degree in Fine Art with graduate work in Textile Design. She worked in NYC as a designer for 10 years designing Fabric and wallpaper. Camille studied Art in NJ\, NYC and Italy and studied Botanical Illustration and Painting at the NY Botanical Gardens with a certified instructor. Her favorite audience to share her love of Botanical art with is her children and grandchildren. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/botanical-drawing-beginners-jan-27/2027-01-05/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/BotanicalPainting.jpg
