BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://ncarboretum.org/event/advanced-botanical-drawing-jan-27/2027-01-05/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270105T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270105T160000
DTSTAMP:20261104T182041Z
CREATED:20261104T182041Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T182041Z
UID:1778780020261-1799154000-1799164800@ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Advanced Botanical Drawing
DESCRIPTION:Advanced Botanical Drawing\nwith Camille Daunno \nFour Sessions: \nTuesdays\, January 5\, 12\, 19\, and 26 |  1 pm – 4 pm \nRegister Here!\nRefine your botanical drawing practice in this advanced-level class designed for artists with prior drawing experience. During this four week series students will strengthen their observational skills while exploring advanced drawing techniques with guided instruction and individualized feedback. Emphasis will be placed on layering\, advanced shading\, and a more involved concentration on light and dark values. Participants should be comfortable with basic drawing fundamentals and come prepared to build upon their existing skills. All materials are provided\, and students will leave with in-progress and completed works and techniques to further their botanical drawing practice. \nCamille Daunno is a retired Art Teacher with an undergraduate degree in Fine Art with graduate work in Textile Design. She worked in NYC as a designer for 10 years designing Fabric and wallpaper. Camille studied Art in NJ\, NYC and Italy and studied Botanical Illustration and Painting at the NY Botanical Gardens with a certified instructor. Her favorite audience to share her love of Botanical art with is her children and grandchildren. \n●  Pre-registration is required for all classes unless otherwise detailed above. \n●  Members: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions. \n●  See a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs. \n●  We are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide. \n●  Follow us on Facebook & Instagram! Or join our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord! \n●  Interested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here. \nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/advanced-botanical-drawing-jan-27/2027-01-05/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/pexels-greta-hoffman-7859251.jpg
END:VEVENT
