X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Jack of the Wood": "https://jackofthewood.com/events/holler-choir-billy-strings-afterparty/", "Where Y'at AVL Music": "https://jackofthewood.com/events/holler-choir-billy-strings-afterparty/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Jackofthewood Events Ics": "https://jackofthewood.com/events/holler-choir-billy-strings-afterparty/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:jackofthewood_events_ics
X-SOURCE:Jack of the Wood, Where Y'at AVL Music
UID:12244@jackofthewood.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270205T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270206T000000
DTSTAMP:20261009T042623Z
URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/holler-choir-billy-strings-afterparty
 /
SUMMARY:Holler Choir Billy Strings Afterparty
DESCRIPTION:\nLed by multi-instrumentalists and songwriters Clint Roberts a
 nd Jackson Grimm\, Asheville’s Holler Choir blends a distinctly Appalach
 ian indie-pop sound with haunting harmonies\, stirring string arrangements
 \, and heart-wrenching ballads—yet rarely conforms to a single genre. Ro
 oted in Old-time\, Americana\, and Bluegrass traditions\, Holler Choir’s
  sound is ultimately singular by design. Alongside Roberts and Grimm\, a r
 otating cast of gifted Appalachian musicians contributes to the group’s 
 recordings and electrifying live performances.\n\n\n\nHoller Choir began d
 uring the recording of Roberts’s 2022 solo EP\,&nbsp\;Mountain Air\, at 
 Asheville’s Crossroads Studios. That fortuitous gathering of roots music
 ians proved to be the genesis of an unmistakable new sound. Produced by Gr
 ammy Award–winning multi-instrumentalist Michael Ashworth of The Steep C
 anyon Rangers\, the five-song EP lit the fuse\, setting Holler Choir on a 
 path to delight audiences throughout the Southeast and beyond. Much of tha
 t same collective reunited to record the band’s 2024 debut full-length a
 lbum\,&nbsp\;Songs Before They Write Themselves\, tracked in the historic 
 church room at Echo Mountain Studios and engineered by Jason Richmond (Ave
 tt Brothers\, Rising Appalachia).\n\n\n\nGrimm officially joined the fold 
 in the summer of 2024 after being invited to collaborate on Holler Choir
 ’s Susto Stringband project\, which reinterprets the indie-rock American
 a songwriting of Susto’s Justin Osborne through old-time and bluegrass l
 enses. As Roberts and Grimm continued working together\, Grimm’s sharp l
 yrical wit and wide-ranging multi-instrumentalism quickly proved to be a p
 owerful addition to the band’s creative core. Holler Choir is slated to 
 release its first collaborative record under this lineup in late 2026 or e
 arly 2027.Music 9pm-12am $10 cover at the door.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://w
 ww.youtube.com/watch?v=cDdeRzmKV8Y\n\n\n\n\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/10/hollerchoir1.jpg
END:VEVENT
